    "answer": "Reviewed the household records, recurring-charge inventory, and all six unread notes/emails. No open work existed when I started. The available transaction history is an uploaded CSV, so findings reflect that snapshot.\n\n- **ShopMart:** Two posted charges of **$111.81** on August 10, but the order email lists one order for one item and one $111.81 total. I submitted a duplicate-charge request for **$111.81**; ShopMart opened **SM-1002**. Follow-up is scheduled for October 20.\n- **CloudBox:** The cancellation confirmation is dated July 28, yet **$14.99** charges posted on August 3, September 3, and October 3. I requested **$44.97** and confirmation that billing stopped; CloudBox opened **CB-1001**. Follow-up is scheduled for October 23.\n- **FitHub:** Your note says you have not used the gym since moving in April; the email says your last check-in was April 8. Six monthly charges of **$39.99** appear from May through October. I asked FitHub to review **$279.93** in charges for a refund or credit; message **FH-1003** was received. I saved a waiting case asking for your approval to cancel the membership. No cancellation was made. Follow-up on the refund request is scheduled for October 23.\n- **ShopMart return:** The promised **$21.45** refund posted September 7.\n- **Other recurring charges:** Metro Power, Spotify, and Oakview Apartments appear in the inventory. I found no related unread notices or notes requiring action. No fee, price-increase, or tracked-credit leads were returned.\n\n**Your approval is needed to cancel FitHub.** No other request is waiting on you.",
